{"id":"mahabharata-13-010","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":10,"title":"दशमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 10 · Counsel given to the unfit","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks whether a man who from friendship gives advice to one of lower birth incurs fault. Bhishma tells of a brahmin who advised a shudra, a forest ascetic, on how to perform the ancestors' rite, and of the king's chaplain, and ends that it is wrong to advise unasked.","kn":"ಮಿತ್ರತ್ವದಿಂದ ಕೆಳ ಜಾತಿಯವನಿಗೆ ಉಪದೇಶ ಮಾಡಿದವನಿಗೆ ದೋಷ ಬರುತ್ತದೆಯೇ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶೂದ್ರ ತಾಪಸನಿಗೆ ಪಿತೃಕಾರ್ಯದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸಿದ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ, ರಾಜಪುರೋಹಿತನ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳಿ ಕೇಳದೆ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸಬಾರದೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि मित्रभाव से निम्न जाति वाले को उपदेश देने वाले को दोष लगता है या नहीं। भीष्म शूद्र तपस्वी को पितृकर्म का उपदेश देने वाले ब्राह्मण और राजपुरोहित की कथा कहकर बताते हैं कि बिना पूछे उपदेश देना अनुचित है।","te":"స్నేహంతో తక్కువ జాతివానికి ఉపదేశం చేసినవానికి దోషం వస్తుందా అని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. శూద్ర తాపసునికి పితృకార్యం గురించి ఉపదేశించిన బ్రాహ్మణుని, రాజపురోహితుని కథ చెప్పి అడగకుండా ఉపదేశించడం తగదని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు.","ta":"நட்பால் தாழ்ந்த குலத்தவனுக்கு உபதேசம் செய்தவனுக்குக் குற்றம் உண்டா என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, சூத்திரத் தவசிக்குப் பித்ரு காரியம் குறித்து உபதேசித்த அந்தணனையும் அரசப் புரோகிதனையும் பற்றிய கதையைக் கூறிக் கேளாமல் உபதேசிக்கக்கூடாது என்று பீஷ்மர் முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"സൗഹൃദംകൊണ്ട് താഴ്ന്ന ജാതിക്കാരന് ഉപദേശം നൽകുന്നവന് കുറ്റമുണ്ടോ എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. വനത്തിൽ തപസ്സു ചെയ്യുന്ന ശൂദ്രനെ പിതൃകർമ്മം എങ്ങനെ ചെയ്യണമെന്ന് ഉപദേശിച്ച ബ്രാഹ്മണന്റെയും, രാജപുരോഹിതന്റെയും കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ചോദിക്കാതെ ഉപദേശം നൽകുന്നത് തെറ്റാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.10; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मित्रसौहृदभावेन उपदेशं करोति यः ।\nजात्यावरस्य राजर्षे दोषस्तस्य भवेन्न वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives instruction out of friendship and goodwill to one of lower birth, royal sage: is there fault in him or not?"}},{"n":2,"text":"एतदिच्छामि तत्त्वेन व्याख्यातुं वै पितामह ।\nसूक्ष्मा गतिर्हि धर्मस्य यत्र मुह्यन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, I wish you to explain this truly, for the course of dharma is subtle, and people are confused about it."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्र ते वर्तयिष्यामि शृणु राजन्यथागमम् ।\nऋषीणां वदतां पूर्वं श्रुतमासीद्यथा मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you about it, king, as the tradition goes, as I heard it long ago when the sages were speaking."}},{"n":4,"text":"उपदेशो न कर्तव्यो जातिहीनस्य कस्यचित् ।\nउपदेशे महान्दोष उपाध्यायस्य भाष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Instruction should not be given to anyone of low birth; great fault is said to attach to the teacher who instructs."}},{"n":5,"text":"निदर्शनमिदं राजञ्शृणु मे भरतर्षभ ।\nदुरुक्तवचने राजन्यथा पूर्वं युधिष्ठिर ।\nब्रह्माश्रमपदे वृत्तं पार्श्वे हिमवतः शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear this illustration from me, king, best of Bharatas, of how ill-spoken words once led to harm, in an event that took place at a hermitage of Brahma on a fair slope of the Himalaya."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्राश्रमपदं पुण्यं नानावृक्षगणायुतम् ।\nबहुगुल्मलताकीर्णं मृगद्विजनिषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That holy hermitage was filled with many kinds of trees and spread with many bushes and creepers, and was frequented by deer and birds."}},{"n":7,"text":"सिद्धचारणसंघुष्टं रम्यं पुष्पितकाननम् ।\nव्रतिभिर्बहुभिः कीर्णं तापसैरुपशोभितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was charming, with flowering groves, resounding with perfected ones and bards, crowded with many men of vows and adorned with ascetics."}},{"n":8,"text":"ब्राह्मणैश्च महाभागैः सूर्यज्वलनसंनिभैः ।\nनियमव्रतसंपन्नैः समाकीर्णं तपस्विभिः ।\nदीक्षितैर्भरतश्रेष्ठ यताहारैः कृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was thronged with fortunate brahmins who shone like the sun and fire, ascetics of discipline and vows, consecrated, moderate in eating and self-mastered."}},{"n":9,"text":"वेदाध्ययनघोषैश्च नादितं भरतर्षभ ।\nवालखिल्यैश्च बहुभिर्यतिभिश्च निषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It echoed with the sound of Vedic study, and was frequented by many Valakhilyas and ascetics."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्र कश्चित्समुत्साहं कृत्वा शूद्रो दयान्वितः ।\nआगतो ह्याश्रमपदं पूजितश्च तपस्विभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A certain Shudra, full of compassion, made up his mind and came to that hermitage and was honored by the ascetics."}},{"n":11,"text":"तांस्तु दृष्ट्वा मुनिगणान्देवकल्पान्महौजसः ।\nवहतो विविधा दीक्षाः संप्रहृष्यत भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those companies of sages, mighty and godlike, observing varied consecrations, he rejoiced greatly."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथास्य बुद्धिरभवत्तपस्ये भरतर्षभ ।\nततोऽब्रवीत्कुलपतिं पादौ संगृह्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a desire for austerity arose in him, and, clasping the feet of the head of the hermitage, he spoke to him."}},{"n":13,"text":"भवत्प्रसादादिच्छामि धर्मं चर्तुं द्विजर्षभ ।\nतन्मां त्वं भगवन्वक्तुं प्रव्राजयितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By your grace, best of brahmins, I wish to practice dharma; please instruct me and let me take up the ascetic life."}},{"n":14,"text":"वर्णावरोऽहं भगवञ्शूद्रो जात्यास्मि सत्तम ।\nशुश्रूषां कर्तुमिच्छामि प्रपन्नाय प्रसीद मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed one, I am of the lowest class, a Shudra by birth, good sir. I wish to serve; be kind to me, who have come to you.\""}},{"text":"कुलपतिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The head of the hermitage said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"न शक्यमिह शूद्रेण लिङ्गमाश्रित्य वर्तितुम् ।\nआस्यतां यदि ते बुद्धिः शुश्रूषानिरतो भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Shudra cannot live here by assuming the marks of an ascetic. If you wish, stay and be devoted to service."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु मुनिना स शूद्रोऽचिन्तयन्नृप ।\nकथमत्र मया कार्यं श्रद्धा धर्मे परा च मे ।\nविज्ञातमेवं भवतु करिष्ये प्रियमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the sage, the Shudra thought, \"What shall I do here? My faith in dharma is supreme. Let it be so, I shall do what pleases my own self.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"गत्वाश्रमपदाद्दूरमुटजं कृतवांस्तु सः ।\nतत्र वेदिं च भूमिं च देवतायतनानि च ।\nनिवेश्य भरतश्रेष्ठ नियमस्थोऽभवत्सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went far from the hermitage and made a hut. There, having set up an altar, a plot of ground and shrines of the gods, he lived happily in discipline."}},{"n":18,"text":"अभिषेकांश्च नियमान्देवतायतनेषु च ।\nबलिं च कृत्वा हुत्वा च देवतां चाप्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He performed ablutions and observances at the shrines, made offerings and oblations, and worshiped the deity."}},{"n":19,"text":"संकल्पनियमोपेतः फलाहारो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nनित्यं संनिहिताभिश्च ओषधीभिः फलैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keeping resolve and discipline, living on fruit and with senses subdued, with herbs and fruits kept always at hand,"}},{"n":20,"text":"अतिथीन्पूजयामास यथावत्समुपागतान् ।\nएवं हि सुमहान्कालो व्यत्यक्रामत्स तस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"he honored guests who came, in due form. In this way a very long time passed for him."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथास्य मुनिरागच्छत्संगत्या वै तमाश्रमम् ।\nसंपूज्य स्वागतेनर्षिं विधिवत्पर्यतोषयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a sage, by chance, came to that hermitage; the Shudra honored him with a welcome and satisfied him by the rite."}},{"n":22,"text":"अनुकूलाः कथाः कृत्वा यथावत्पर्यपृच्छत ।\nऋषिः परमतेजस्वी धर्मात्मा संयतेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage, brilliant, righteous and with senses restrained, conversed pleasantly and asked about him in due form."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवं स बहुशस्तस्य शूद्रस्य भरतर्षभ ।\nसोऽगच्छदाश्रममृषिः शूद्रं द्रष्टुं नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way, best of Bharatas, that sage came many times to the hermitage to see the Shudra."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथ तं तापसं शूद्रः सोऽब्रवीद्भरतर्षभ ।\nपितृकार्यं करिष्यामि तत्र मेऽनुग्रहं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Shudra said to that ascetic, \"I wish to perform a rite for my ancestors; please favor me in it.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"बाढमित्येव तं विप्र उवाच भरतर्षभ ।\nशुचिर्भूत्वा स शूद्रस्तु तस्यर्षेः पाद्यमानयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Very well,\" the brahmin said to him. Then the Shudra, having made himself pure, brought water for the sage's feet."}},{"n":26,"text":"अथ दर्भांश्च वन्याश्च ओषधीर्भरतर्षभ ।\nपवित्रमासनं चैव बृसीं च समुपानयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He then brought darbha grass and forest herbs, a purified seat and a cushion."}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ दक्षिणमावृत्य बृसीं परमशीर्षिकाम् ।\nकृतामन्यायतो दृष्ट्वा ततस्तमृषिरब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the cushion placed with its head toward the south, wrongly laid, the sage said to him:"}},{"n":28,"text":"कुरुष्वैतां पूर्वशीर्षां भव चोदङ्मुखः शुचिः ।\nस च तत्कृतवाञ्शूद्रः सर्वं यदृषिरब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Place it with its head to the east, and be pure and face north.\" The Shudra did all as the sage said."}},{"n":29,"text":"यथोपदिष्टं मेधावी दर्भादींस्तान्यथातथम् ।\nहव्यकव्यविधिं कृत्स्नमुक्तं तेन तपस्विना ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man did the darbha grass and the rest just as instructed, and the whole procedure for offerings to gods and ancestors that the ascetic told him."}},{"n":30,"text":"ऋषिणा पितृकार्ये च स च धर्मपथे स्थितः ।\nपितृकार्ये कृते चापि विसृष्टः स जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage was in the ancestors' rite and the Shudra was on the path of dharma; when the ancestors' rite was done, the sage was dismissed and left."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथ दीर्घस्य कालस्य स तप्यञ्शूद्रतापसः ।\nवने पञ्चत्वमगमत्सुकृतेन च तेन वै ।\nअजायत महाराजराजवंशे महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long time, the Shudra ascetic, practicing austerity in the forest, died; and by that merit he was born, great king, as a very radiant prince in a royal line."}},{"n":32,"text":"तथैव स ऋषिस्तात कालधर्ममवाप्य ह ।\nपुरोहितकुले विप्र आजातो भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage too, son, having met the law of time, was born as a brahmin in the household of a royal chaplain, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":33,"text":"एवं तौ तत्र संभूतावुभौ शूद्रमुनी तदा ।\nक्रमेण वर्धितौ चापि विद्यासु कुशलावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So those two, the Shudra and the sage, were born there and grew up in due order, both skilled in the sciences."}},{"n":34,"text":"अथर्ववेदे वेदे च बभूवर्षिः सुनिश्चितः ।\nकल्पप्रयोगे चोत्पन्ने ज्योतिषे च परं गतः ।\nसख्ये चापि परा प्रीतिस्तयोश्चापि व्यवर्धत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage became well versed in the Atharva Veda and the Vedas, in ritual practice, and went to the farthest end of astronomy; and the deep affection between the two also grew."}},{"n":35,"text":"पितर्युपरते चापि कृतशौचः स भारत ।\nअभिषिक्तः प्रकृतिभी राजपुत्रः स पार्थिवः ।\nअभिषिक्तेन स ऋषिरभिषिक्तः पुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his father died, Bharata, the prince, having done the purifications, was consecrated king by the subjects; and the sage was consecrated chaplain by the consecrated king."}},{"n":36,"text":"स तं पुरोधाय सुखमवसद्भरतर्षभ ।\nराज्यं शशास धर्मेण प्रजाश्च परिपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made him his chaplain, the king lived happily, ruling by dharma and protecting the people."}},{"n":37,"text":"पुण्याहवाचने नित्यं धर्मकार्येषु चासकृत् ।\nउत्स्मयन्प्राहसच्चापि दृष्ट्वा राजा पुरोहितम् ।\nएवं स बहुशो राजन्पुरोधसमुपाहसत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whenever the auspicious-day blessing was recited and in religious works again and again, the king would smile and laugh on seeing the chaplain. So, king, he laughed at his chaplain many times."}},{"n":38,"text":"लक्षयित्वा पुरोधास्तु बहुशस्तं नराधिपम् ।\nउत्स्मयन्तं च सततं दृष्ट्वासौ मन्युमानभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having noticed that the king smiled constantly, the chaplain became angry."}},{"n":39,"text":"अथ शून्ये पुरोधास्तु सह राज्ञा समागतः ।\nकथाभिरनुकूलाभी राजानमभिरामयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in private, the chaplain met the king and pleased him with agreeable talk."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीन्नरेन्द्रं स पुरोधा भरतर्षभ ।\nवरमिच्छाम्यहं त्वेकं त्वया दत्तं महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the chaplain said to the king, best of Bharatas, \"Radiant one, I wish to ask one boon from you.\""}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"वराणां ते शतं दद्यां किमुतैकं द्विजोत्तम ।\nस्नेहाच्च बहुमानाच्च नास्त्यदेयं हि मे तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would give you a hundred boons, best of brahmins, much less one; out of affection and esteem, there is nothing I would not give you."}},{"text":"पुरोहित उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The chaplain said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"एकं वै वरमिच्छामि यदि तुष्टोऽसि पार्थिव ।\nयद्ददासि महाराज सत्यं तद्वद मानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I want one boon, king, if you are pleased: tell me the truth, great king, and not a falsehood, about what you give."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"बाढमित्येव तं राजा प्रत्युवाच युधिष्ठिर ।\nयदि ज्ञास्यामि वक्ष्यामि अजानन्न तु संवदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Very well,\" said the king to him, Yudhishthira. \"If I know, I will say; if I do not know, I will not speak.\""}},{"text":"पुरोहित उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The chaplain said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"पुण्याहवाचने नित्यं धर्मकृत्येषु चासकृत् ।\nशान्तिहोमेषु च सदा किं त्वं हससि वीक्ष्य माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the auspicious-day blessing is spoken, in religious works again and again, and in rites of pacification, why do you laugh on seeing me?"}},{"n":45,"text":"सव्रीडं वै भवति हि मनो मे हसता त्वया ।\nकामया शापितो राजन्नान्यथा वक्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mind is ashamed at your laughing, king. I adjure you by my wish; you must not answer otherwise."}},{"n":46,"text":"भाव्यं हि कारणेनात्र न ते हास्यमकारणम् ।\nकौतूहलं मे सुभृशं तत्त्वेन कथयस्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There must be a reason here, for you do not laugh without cause. My curiosity is great; tell me truly."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":47,"text":"एवमुक्ते त्वया विप्र यदवाच्यं भवेदपि ।\nअवश्यमेव वक्तव्यं शृणुष्वैकमना द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since you have said this, brahmin, though it may be unspeakable, it must certainly be told. Listen with a single mind, twice-born."}},{"n":48,"text":"पूर्वदेहे यथा वृत्तं तन्निबोध द्विजोत्तम ।\nजातिं स्मराम्यहं ब्रह्मन्नवधानेन मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understand, best of brahmins, what happened in my former body. I remember my birth, brahmin; listen with attention."}},{"n":49,"text":"शूद्रोऽहमभवं पूर्वं तापसो भृशसंयुतः ।\nऋषिरुग्रतपास्त्वं च तदाभूर्द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was formerly a Shudra, an ascetic of great discipline, and you at that time, best of brahmins, were a sage of fierce austerity."}},{"n":50,"text":"प्रीयता हि तदा ब्रह्मन्ममानुग्रहबुद्धिना ।\nपितृकार्ये त्वया पूर्वमुपदेशः कृतोऽनघ ।\nबृस्यां दर्भेषु हव्ये च कव्ये च मुनिसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being kind then, brahmin, with a mind to favor me, you gave me instruction at the ancestors' rite, faultless one, about the cushion, the darbha grass, and the offerings to gods and ancestors."}},{"n":51,"text":"एतेन कर्मदोषेण पुरोधास्त्वमजायथाः ।\nअहं राजा च विप्रेन्द्र पश्य कालस्य पर्ययम् ।\nमत्कृते ह्युपदेशेन त्वया प्राप्तमिदं फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that fault of action you were born as a chaplain. I am king, and you are a brahmin; see the turn of time. By giving instruction on my account, you obtained this fruit."}},{"n":52,"text":"एतस्मात्कारणाद्ब्रह्मन्प्रहसे त्वां द्विजोत्तम ।\nन त्वां परिभवन्ब्रह्मन्प्रहसामि गुरुर्भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason, brahmin, I laugh at you, best of the twice-born, not out of contempt, for you are my teacher."}},{"n":53,"text":"विपर्ययेण मे मन्युस्तेन संतप्यते मनः ।\nजातिं स्मराम्यहं तुभ्यमतस्त्वां प्रहसामि वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mind is troubled and pained at the reversal; because I remember my birth, I laugh at you."}},{"n":54,"text":"एवं तवोग्रं हि तप उपदेशेन नाशितम् ।\nपुरोहितत्वमुत्सृज्य यतस्व त्वं पुनर्भवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way your fierce austerity was destroyed by instruction. Give up the chaplaincy and strive in your next birth."}},{"n":55,"text":"इतस्त्वमधमामन्यां मा योनिं प्राप्स्यसे द्विज ।\nगृह्यतां द्रविणं विप्र पूतात्मा भव सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not fall into some other lower womb from here, brahmin. Take wealth, brahmin, and be of purified self, good sir."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":56,"text":"ततो विसृष्टो राज्ञा तु विप्रो दानान्यनेकशः ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्यो ददौ वित्तं भूमिं ग्रामांश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, dismissed by the king, the brahmin gave many gifts to brahmins, wealth, land and villages everywhere."}},{"n":57,"text":"कृच्छ्राणि चीर्त्वा च ततो यथोक्तानि द्विजोत्तमः ।\nतीर्थानि चाभिगत्वा वै दानानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of the twice-born performed the penances as prescribed, visited holy places and gave gifts of many kinds."}},{"n":58,"text":"दत्त्वा गाश्चैव विप्राणां पूतात्मा सोऽभवद्द्विजः ।\nतमेव चाश्रमं गत्वा चचार विपुलं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given cows to brahmins, he became purified in self; and going to that same hermitage, he practiced great austerity."}},{"n":59,"text":"ततः सिद्धिं परां प्राप्तो ब्राह्मणो राजसत्तम ।\nसंमतश्चाभवत्तेषामाश्रमेऽऽश्रमवासिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that brahmin, best of kings, attained supreme perfection and was honored by the dwellers of that hermitage."}},{"n":60,"text":"एवं प्राप्तो महत्कृच्छ्रमृषिः स नृपसत्तम ।\nब्राह्मणेन न वक्तव्यं तस्माद्वर्णावरे जने ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way that sage suffered great hardship, best of kings. Therefore a brahmin should not speak to those of lower class."}},{"n":61,"text":"वर्जयेदुपदेशं च सदैव ब्राह्मणो नृप ।\nउपदेशं हि कुर्वाणो द्विजः कृच्छ्रमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin, king, should always avoid giving instruction; a twice-born who gives instruction may fall into hardship."}},{"n":62,"text":"एषितव्यं सदा वाचा नृपेण द्विजसत्तमात् ।\nन प्रवक्तव्यमिह हि किंचिद्वर्णावरे जने ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should always seek counsel in words from the best of brahmins; nothing should be taught here to those of lower class."}},{"n":63,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः क्षत्रिया वैश्यास्त्रयो वर्णा द्विजातयः ।\nएतेषु कथयन्राजन्ब्राह्मणो न प्रदुष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins, Kshatriyas and Vaishyas, the three twice-born classes: a brahmin who speaks to them, king, is not tainted."}},{"n":64,"text":"तस्मात्सद्भिर्न वक्तव्यं कस्यचित्किंचिदग्रतः ।\nसूक्ष्मा गतिर्हि धर्मस्य दुर्ज्ञेया ह्यकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the good should not say anything to anyone beforehand; the course of dharma is subtle and hard for the unrefined to know."}},{"n":65,"text":"तस्मान्मौनानि मुनयो दीक्षां कुर्वन्ति चादृताः ।\nदुरुक्तस्य भयाद्राजन्नानुभाषन्ति किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore sages observe silence and honor consecration; out of fear of ill-spoken words, king, they say nothing."}},{"n":66,"text":"धार्मिका गुणसंपन्नाः सत्यार्जवपरायणाः ।\nदुरुक्तवाचाभिहताः प्राप्नुवन्तीह दुष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Righteous people, virtuous, devoted to truth and honesty, are struck by ill-spoken words and reap evil here."}},{"n":67,"text":"उपदेशो न कर्तव्यः कदाचिदपि कस्यचित् ।\nउपदेशाद्धि तत्पापं ब्राह्मणः समवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Instruction should never be given to anyone at any time; by instruction a brahmin would incur that sin."}},{"n":68,"text":"विमृश्य तस्मात्प्राज्ञेन वक्तव्यं धर्ममिच्छता ।\nसत्यानृतेन हि कृत उपदेशो हिनस्ति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the wise man who wishes for dharma should speak only after reflection; instruction given with truth mixed with falsehood harms."}},{"n":69,"text":"वक्तव्यमिह पृष्टेन विनिश्चित्य विपर्ययम् ।\nस चोपदेशः कर्तव्यो येन धर्ममवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When asked, one should speak here after determining the reverse; and the instruction to be given is that by which one may gain dharma."}},{"n":70,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातमुपदेशे कृते सति ।\nमहान्क्लेशो हि भवति तस्मान्नोपदिशेत्क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you all this: when instruction is given, great trouble results; so one should not instruct anywhere."}}]}]}